From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:54:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tools/asahi: run the J713 sleep tests from the
 host-test runner

The J713 native radio and docked deep-sleep series added seventeen host
tests without listing them in run-host-tests.py, and the runner fails a
run on any test it doesn't list. List them.

Three of them import sleep_test_utils from their own directory, which
python3 -I, as the runner runs every test, leaves off sys.path: put it
back. t8132-usb4-policy-tests.py needed the Python libfdt module and
trees built beforehand. Build the T8132 platform data and the J713 and
J715 trees with this tree's dtc instead, as the other device-tree tests
do, and read them with a small flattened-tree reader. On the trees
built here it finds the same ten USB4 PMGR providers per board as the
libfdt version did, its reader agrees with libfdt on every node and
property, and disabling any one of the ten in the policy fails it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 19de60a3ee67692d5cde5489be186ac9bd6d3dfb)
